# Nightly backup of the shop database: runs scripts/backup.sh at 03:00, which
# writes backups/shop_<UTC timestamp>.dump plus its .check sidecar, and appends
# the run's output to backups/backup.log.
#
# Timezone: cron uses the host's local timezone, so 03:00 is host time. The
# dump's file name is in UTC regardless.
#
# Install. `crontab backup.cron` would REPLACE your whole crontab, so append:
#   (crontab -l 2>/dev/null; cat backup.cron) | crontab -
# On Linux you can instead copy it to /etc/cron.d/m_api-backup; files there need
# a user field before the command (e.g. `0 3 * * * deploy cd …`).
# Adjust /opt/m_api below to the repo's absolute path on install.
#
# Secrets: backup.sh connects with MIGRATIONS_DB_URL (the schema owner, directly
# to Postgres), which with-secrets.sh loads from the vault; the S3 upload (#26)
# will need keys from it too. An unattended job can't do an interactive vault
# login, so production needs a machine identity token for Infisical; that isn't
# set up yet.
#
# Keep % out of the command line: cron turns it into a newline. The date is
# built inside backup.sh for that reason.

# PATH is set on the command, not as a NAME=value line: appended to an existing
# crontab, that line would apply to every job below it too. Docker Desktop for
# Mac installs docker in /usr/local/bin; most Linux in /usr/bin. mkdir comes
# first: the log redirect needs backups/ before backup.sh gets to create it,
# and on a fresh install it doesn't exist yet.
0 3 * * * cd /opt/m_api && mkdir -p backups && PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin bash scripts/with-secrets.sh prod bash scripts/backup.sh >> backups/backup.log 2>&1
